  "question": "In the advanced biomechanical analysis of countermovement jumps (CMJ), the orientation of the ground reaction force (GRF) vector relative to the knee joint center during the eccentric (landing) phase is a critical determinant of joint integrity. If the resultant GRF vector is projected anterior to the center of rotation of the knee joint during this phase, which of the following biomechanical consequences is most accurately predicted regarding knee joint loading and injury risk?",
